  "static_route_policies": ["unselected", "static", "dynamic"],
  "static_route_refusals": ["unverifiable", "unnamed_model", "unlisted_model", "ineligible_model", "effort_not_configurable", "unsupported_effort", "unsupported_context_tier"],
  "static_route_notes": {
    "policy": "Contract 2.8. The file-level contract_version above stays at the revision that first described the measured tier; these Static route cases arrived at 2.8 and say so here rather than moving a declaration that belongs to a different decision. The Route policy is SELECTED, never inherited. `unselected` is the absence of a decision and MUST keep every legacy behaviour -- the hardcoded roster gates, the built-in escalation rung, the historical event stream -- byte-for-byte. Only `static` activates the cases below. A Runner MUST NOT reinterpret an existing Config as though the policy had always been in force, and MUST NOT read the absence of a policy as a choice of one.",
    "verifiable_placement": "The harness whose answer counts is the one the WORK SESSION runs under. Where an Execution host opens its sessions on a machine that authenticates as itself, the orchestrator's own listing describes a different installation under a different identity, and a Runner MUST refuse that combination before work rather than report a local read as that placement's verdict. Only a placement whose sessions run under the Run's own authenticated harness is verifiable.",
  "authority": "Under `static` the authority is the AUTHENTICATED HARNESS THIS RUN SPAWNS -- its own model listing, read fresh. A Runner MUST NOT validate a Static route against a hardcoded roster, a published plan or licence catalogue, or another CLI installation, and MUST NOT satisfy the read from a cache held across the Run: a stale answer is the failure this rule exists to prevent, not a cheaper version of it. Reading eligibility MUST NOT rewrite billing provenance already recorded for the Run.",
    "refuse_never_rescue": "Every verdict other than `accepted` ends the Run BEFORE any work, naming the selected settings. A Runner MUST NOT drop an unsupported effort, downgrade an unoffered context tier, or substitute a backend default and call the result a route: a Static route is honoured exactly or not at all.",
    "effort_dial_versus_effort_value": "`efforts: null` is the harness's own statement that the model has NO EFFORT DIAL, and a route on such a model MUST send no effort argument at all. That is a different fact from a model whose dial offers the value `none`, which MUST be sent as a value. A Runner that collapses the two either sends `none` to a model that cannot read it, or omits an effort the operator explicitly selected.",
    "unverifiable_is_not_empty": "`harness: null` is a capability read that did not complete. It is `unverifiable` -- NOT an empty harness, NOT a reason to fall back to a roster, and NOT a reason to proceed. A Runner MUST NOT treat an unanswered harness as agreement.",
    "static_is_fixed": "A Static route stays fixed for an Agent and across every permitted retry. A Runner MUST NOT promote it to a different model or effort unless the operator explicitly configured an escalation rung: a rung a Runner ships by default is not consent. Attempt and Strike accounting is unchanged either way.",
    "scope": "These cases validate ONE route. A Run validates every route its Config holds -- the run-wide default, each [routing] entry, and an explicitly configured escalation rung -- before it picks up any issue, so a route that is never exercised is still refused at the start rather than mid-Run."
  },
  "static_route_cases": [
    {
      "id": "a-complete-verified-route-is-honoured",
      "note": "Model eligible, effort on the dial, tier offered. Nothing to rescue.",
      "harness": [{"model": "synthetic-fancy-9", "eligible": true, "efforts": ["low", "high", "max"], "context_tiers": ["default", "long_context"]}],
